A persistent effect, so if we imagine it as a covariate some animals that have been caught at least once in their life would have a '1' for recap on occasion 1, whilst animals which had never been caught in their life would be '0' on first capture. I have tried it as a covariate effect; however, when I copy the effect of model 'b', i.e. pretending animals were naive on occasion 1, as a covariate effect I get a quite different answer to model b. Hope that makes sense.

